 "description": "Precomputed result of recipe monthly_departure 1.0.0 on bundle_s2_ndvi_monthly_ait_bouguemez: 58 of 84 periods have a departure. The reference is a short period (2019 to 2025), not a climate normal. A departure describes how this month differs from other years here; it does not say why. The spatial IQR is variability across pixels, not a confidence interval. In winter months the accepted pixels favour the valley floor and south-facing slopes, because snow and shade remove the others; the area value then describes those pixels, not the whole catchment.",
